From: Nobara Project <packages@nobaraproject.org>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 12:20:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Detect i686 as x86 in CMake architecture normalization

Fedora i686 builds report CMAKE_LIBRARY_ARCHITECTURE/CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR
values such as i686-redhat-linux-gnu or i686.  Upstream only recognizes i386
among the 32-bit x86 names, so the normalized target architecture becomes
UNKNOWN.

That leaves VVENC_ENABLE_X86_SIMD enabled, but prevents the AVX2 x86 SIMD
sources from being added to libvvenc.  InitX86.cpp can still reference the
AVX2 init templates on real x86, causing unresolved symbols when apps link
against the shared library.

Treat the common i386/i486/i586/i686 family as X86.
---
 cmake/modules/vvencCompilerSupport.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/modules/vvencCompilerSupport.cmake b/cmake/modules/vvencCompilerSupport.cmake
index 5d9980d..e1d9010 100644
--- a/cmake/modules/vvencCompilerSupport.cmake
+++ b/cmake/modules/vvencCompilerSupport.cmake
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@ function( _append_cpu_type_guess output_list input_str )
   set( ret ${${output_list}} )
 
   string( TOLOWER "${input_str}" input_lower )
-  if( ${input_lower} MATCHES "x86\|i386\|x64\|win32\|amd64" )
+  if( ${input_lower} MATCHES "x86\|i[3-6]86\|x64\|win32\|amd64" )
     list( APPEND ret "X86" )
   elseif( ${input_lower} MATCHES "aarch64\|arm64")
     list( APPEND ret "AARCH64" )
